    SimpleSal Soft Open publishment

  This publishment implements the changes required to transition from the state of
      big 'D', "Developing software" to the state of big 'P', "Publishing software".

  Published software is coherent within the managed object or Blob.  Coherence means
  the contents of the Blob in all forms (source files, algorithms, help documents)
  relate to this instance of the software being published, using the same concepts.

------------------------------------------

  Why is the human version is "v1.0.0"?  Modern conventions call for this form. Also, a reason is:

    While not the first commit to the repository, this publishment is the first to be made public.

  SimpleSal Apps published to their repo will declare the TSC LLC or Human version they require.
     TSC LLC philosophy has a rule against publishing with not-yet-published "v0.x" software.

  The completion of development to v1.0.0 included several SimpleSal Apps, and more important,
     keeping them current with the SimpleSal software version.  All part of a major publishment.

  The collection of software and documents within SimpleSal, and a collection of SimpleSal Apps
  that make use of the software, are considered to be coherent.  A collection worthy of support.

